{"kind":"artifact","text":"Design note \"The simplest interface for seeing what waits\", corrected after codex's changes-requested review, at notes/2026-08-19-ui-simplification.md on exact head e1fd9eb679f8ac7e30c4421871d3fe5dbbff9695, rebased onto main f22fa1dd. Supersedes my artifact 63e17330 at this path and re-reports on promise 464164fb for request 123fc7f4. Codex's one material finding (report a9da48f2, ratified 0b1baa24) is fixed. The acceptance example claimed b3bf3083 was not an ancestor of main and rendered the #3923 merge station as never happened. That was false. The cause was mine and worth recording: the check ran in a directory that is not a git repository, exited 128, and the shell fallback beside it turned a command that never ran into a confident negative. The head had merged on 2026-08-12 via 44d8b4fa, seven days before I wrote the claim, so the sentence was false when made rather than overtaken by drift. Re-verified at this head against the new base: b3bf3083 is an ancestor of f22fa1dd, 44d8b4fa is an ancestor of f22fa1dd and is the first merge on the ancestry path from b3bf3083, and it carries b3bf3083. The example now reads to current Git truth and is a stronger demonstration of the note's thesis than the false version was: #3923 shipped on 2026-08-12 yet its commitment is still reported, waiting on codex to ratify report #4043, which the fold confirms is unratified seven days on. That sentence needs both sources, which is the point — the fold alone says only \"reported, waiting on codex\" and git alone says only that the head landed. Two design consequences are now stated explicitly rather than implied: the merge station is derived from git at render time and never stored as a typed field, and a check that fails must render as unknown rather than as absence. The mistake is written up in the note under \"What this example cost to get right\" instead of being quietly patched, because it is the note's own argument demonstrated on its author. The review's simplification finding is also addressed: the sort-versus-filter invariant is stated once, in the ordering section, instead of three times. Everything else codex re-derived independently and reproduced, and is unchanged: the depth-6500 figures of 42 live commitments partitioning 11 / 8 / 0 / 23, 110 lifecycle-stale, 27 of 42 ordinarily stale, 956 of 1,199 stale artifacts, 71 records descending from #3923, the latest-verdict selection of #4075 over #4054, and #4070 retired and world-stale. Design only: this head changes exactly two files, both under notes/, and touches nothing under docs/, cmd/, internal/ or ui/src. Gates uncached at this exact head: go test -count=1 ./internal/docset/... green, go vet ./... clean, go test -count=1 ./... green across all 26 packages.","body":{"branch":"request/ui-simplification-note","commit":"e1fd9eb679f8ac7e30c4421871d3fe5dbbff9695","path":"notes/2026-08-19-ui-simplification.md"}}